Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `items` was consumed by the binding `kept`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/copies_explicit_share_use_after_move.jet:8:13
    |
  8 |     print("{items.len()} {kept.len()}")
    |             ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/copies_explicit_share_use_after_move.jet:7:13
    |
  7 |     kept := items
    |             ^^^^^ `items` moved to the binding `kept` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `items` after the move, or give the binding `kept` a copy with `items.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
